  "worked_solution": "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $6|10$ and $6|18.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{6|10}_{⏟}}_{M}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{6|18}_{⏟}}_{P}\n$$\n\nthat is, $M∧P.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $11$ is prime and odd. This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{11\\text{ is prime}}_{⏟}}_{N}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{11\\text{ is odd }}_{⏟}}_{Q},\n$$\n\nthat is, $N∧Q.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{6|10\\text{ and }6|18}_{⏟}}_{M\\,∧\\,P}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{11\\text{ is prime }\\text{and}\\text{ odd }}_{⏟}}_{N\\,∧\\,Q},\n$$\n\nthat is, $(M∧P)∨(N∧Q).$",
